.TH BAUX-BOT 1 "December 12, 2025" "RoxieOS v0.1" "BAUX-BOT Manual"
.SH NAME
baux-bot \- AI-powered development assistant for RoxieOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B baux-bot.sh
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B baux-bot
is an intelligent AI assistant specifically designed for RoxieOS development. It maintains a comprehensive understanding of the entire codebase through continuous RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) scanning, providing context-aware assistance for development tasks.
.PP
The bot automatically scans the /src directory tree, builds a knowledge base of all source files, git repositories, and recent changes, then uses this context to provide accurate, codebase-aware responses.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Real-time Codebase Awareness
Continuously monitors /src for changes and rebuilds its knowledge base automatically
.TP
.B Multi-Model Support
Prioritizes deepseek-coder:33b, falls back through qwen2.5:7b, llama3.2:3b, gemma2:2b, phi3:3.8b, smollm2:135m
.TP
.B Persistent Context
Maintains ~2000-line RAG file with git status, recent commits, and latest source files
.TP
.B Interactive Mode
Runs continuously until explicitly exited with the word "exit"
.TP
.B Comprehensive Logging
Logs all interactions to /var/log/baux-bot/current.log
.SH USAGE
.SS Starting the Bot
.nf
$ ./baux-bot.sh
BAUX BOT v6.2 alive — model: deepseek-coder:33b — /src is law
Type anything. Only the word 'exit' kills me.

you >
.fi
.SS Example Interaction
.nf
you > how do I add a new keybind to bauxwm?
BAUX BOT: To add a new keybind to bauxwm, modify the config.h file in the dwm source directory. Look for the keys[] array and add your binding following the existing pattern...

you > show me the current tmux configuration
BAUX BOT: The current tmux configuration is in /usr/local/share/tmux/baux.conf. Key features include:
- Leader key set to C-Space
- Vi-style navigation
- Session resurrection enabled
- Custom status bar with BAUX branding
.fi
.SS Special Commands
.TP
.B exit
Terminate the bot session
.TP
.B (any other input)
Send query to AI model with full codebase context
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS Environment Variables
.TP
.B SRC_ROOT
Root directory to scan (default: /src)
.TP
.B MODEL_PREF
Array of preferred models in priority order
.SS Directory Structure
.nf
/var/log/baux-bot/          # Log files
  └── current.log           # Current session log
/var/lib/baux-bot/rag/      # RAG knowledge base
  └── current.txt           # Current codebase snapshot
.fi
.SH MODEL SELECTION
The bot automatically selects the best available model from:
.PP
1. deepseek-coder:33b (preferred for coding tasks)
.br
2. qwen2.5:7b (general purpose)
.br
3. llama3.2:3b (fallback)
.br
4. gemma2:2b (lightweight)
.br
5. phi3:3.8b (Microsoft Phi)
.br
6. smollm2:135m (minimal fallback)
.PP
Models are automatically pulled if not present.
.SH RAG SYSTEM
.SS Automatic Rebuilding
The bot monitors the source tree and rebuilds the RAG when files change:
.nf
- Git repository status and recent commits
- Latest 50 source files (*.sh, *.c, *.lua, *.conf, *.md, *.vim)
- Full content of recent files (last 200 lines each)
.fi
.SS Manual Rebuilding
The RAG rebuilds automatically when source files are modified. No manual intervention required.
.SH INTEGRATION
.SS TMUX Integration
Designed to work within BAUX TMUX sessions, providing context-aware assistance during development.
.SS BVI Integration
Can be called from within the BVI editor for code-specific questions.
.SS BAUX Ecosystem
Fully integrated with the BAUX session manager and distributed storage system.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Development Questions
.nf
you > how does the baux session resurrection work?
you > what changed in the latest commit?
you > explain the tmux configuration structure
.fi
.SS Code Assistance
.nf
you > write a function to parse baux config files
you > debug this tmux error: [error message]
you > optimize this shell script for performance
.fi
.SS System Questions
.nf
you > how do I add a new package to the ports tree?
you > explain the debian packaging workflow
you > what are the current build dependencies?
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.SS Common Issues
.TP
.B "ERROR: no /src/roxieos"
Ensure the source tree is mounted at /src or set SRC_ROOT environment variable
.TP
.B "ollama connection failed"
Check that Ollama service is running and models are available
.TP
.B "RAG rebuild slow"
Normal on HDD storage; SSD systems are much faster
.SS Logs
Check /var/log/baux-bot/current.log for detailed error information and interaction history.
